   <h2>The Third Branch of the First TANDARA Family</h2>

<h3>Ante Tandara Ivanov (born c. 1730 – ...)</h3>

<p>Ante Tandara, probably about one year younger than Petar, was the son of Ivan Tandara. He married Matija Brnas, and they had three sons: Ante, Filip, and Pavao, and three daughters: Jaka, Luca, and Ruža. There is no additional information about Pavao apart from his birth record.</p>

<h2>Sub-branch of Ante, son of Ante</h2>

<h3>Ante Antin</h3>

<p>Ante, the eldest son of Ante Ivanov, married Matija Jukić in 1801. They had three sons: Lovro, Mijo, and Petar, and five daughters: Pera, Ruža, Antica, Iva, and Marija. There is no additional information about Petar apart from his birth record.</p>

<p>According to the 1819 population census, Ante lived in Zavelim, while his brother Filip lived in Ričice. Their descendants later spread across Croatia, Europe, and Canada.</p>

<h3>Lovro Antin</h3>

<p>He married Matija Sičenica. They had two sons: Marijan and Križan.</p>

<h3>Marijan Lovrin</h3>

<p>He married Matija Kovač. They had four sons: Jure, Marko, Stipan, and Jozo, and three daughters: Iva, Mara, and Matija.</p>

<p>There is no record of Stipan apart from his birth entry, so it is assumed he either died young or moved away.</p>

<p>The descendants of Marijan through his sons Marko and Jure are known by the nickname <strong>Lovrinovići</strong>. The nickname comes from Marijan’s father Lovro. Today they live in Popovača, Sarajevo, and Stobreč.</p>

<h3>Marko Marijanov</h3>

<p>He married Božica Pušić. They had one son, Mirko, and one daughter, Iva.</p>

<h3>Mirko Markov</h3>

<p>He married Anica Kliić. They had two sons, Milan and Vladimir, who died at the age of 14, and three daughters: Dragica, Marija, and Nediljka.</p>

<h3>Milan Markov</h3>

<p>He married Svjetlana Trifunović. They had two sons: Vladimir and Dalibor.</p>

<p>Vladimir Milanov married Claire Tacher. They have a son, Alexander James, and live in London.</p>

<p>Dalibor married Amela Nezirović. They have a son, Damir, and a daughter, Tea. They live in Sarajevo.</p>

<h3>Križan Lovrin</h3>

<p>He married Pera Budimir. They had 15 children, seven of whom died before the age of ten.</p>

<p>An interesting fact is that Križan’s second son Ilija was killed by a bull.</p>

<p>Descendants of Križan through his sons Mate, Ante, Ivan, and Jure are known as <strong>Križanovići</strong>, and today live in Zagreb, Đakovo, Kutjevo, Bektež, Strizivojna, Vrpolje, and several European countries.</p>

<h3>Mate Križanov</h3>

<p>The eldest son of Križan, he married Iva Pirić. They had three sons: Mijo, Marijan, and Jozo, and two daughters: Mara and Matija. Mijo never married.</p> 
<h3>Marijan Matin</h3>

<p>Marijan married Anica Maras. They had four sons: Ante, Jozo, Mate, and Ivan, and one daughter, Mara.</p>

<h3>Ante Marijanov</h3>

<p>From his first marriage to Elizabeta Miletić, Ante had a son, Darko, and a daughter, Gordana. In his second marriage to Ana Kajtar, he had no children.</p>

<p>Darko and his family live in Germany.</p>

<h3>Jozo Marijanov</h3>

<p>Jozo never married.</p>

<h3>Mate Marijanov</h3>

<p>Mate married Anica Bogdanović. They had a son, Alen, and a daughter, Laura.</p>

<p>Alen and his family live in Slavonski Brod.</p>

<h3>Ivan Marijanov</h3>

<p>The fourth son of Marijan, Ivan married Ljiljana Cobović. They have a son, Marijan, and two daughters, Lana and Paulina.</p>

<p>The family lives in Đakovo, where Ivan runs his own law office.</p>

<h3>Jozo Matin</h3>

<p>The youngest son of Mate and Iva Pirić, Jozo married Jaka Kliić. They had three sons: Mijo, Jozo, and Ivan, and one daughter, Mara.</p>

<p>Jozo was killed during the Second World War. The family of his son Mijo now lives in Bektež near Kutjevo.</p>

<h3>Mijo Jozin</h3>

<p>Mijo lives in Bektež near Kutjevo and has three daughters.</p>

<h3>Jozo Jozin</h3>

<p>Jozo lives in Slovenia. He has a son, Marijan, and a daughter, Romana.</p>

<p>Marijan has a son, Martin, and two daughters, Tamara, and Petricija.</p>

<h3>Ante Križanov</h3>

<p>The third son of Križan, Ante married Iva Trogrlić. They had one son, Stipan, and two daughters, Jela and Mara.</p>

<p>Stipan moved to Serbia, and it is unknown whether he had descendants.</p>

<h3>Ivan Križanov</h3>

<p>Ivan, the eighth son of Križan, married Ruža Serdarušić. They had three sons: Ante (who died at age five), Križan, and Marijan (who died in childhood), and two daughters, Mara and Ana.</p>

<h3>Križan Ivanov</h3>

<p>Križan married Marica Pušić. They had one son, Ivan.</p>

<p>Križan was killed in Zagreb in 1944.</p>

<h3>Ivan Križanov</h3>

<p>Ivan married twice.</p>

<p>From his first marriage to Dragica Dragun, he had a son named Križan.</p>

<h3>Križan Ivanov (Vrpolje branch)</h3>

<p>Križan married Ljerka Maričić. They have two sons, Toni and Dinko, and live in Vrpolje.</p>

<p>From his second marriage to Anka Nikolić, Ivan had two daughters, Biljana and Belina.</p>

<h3>Jure Križanov</h3>

<p>Jure, the ninth son of Križan, married three times.</p>

<p>His first wife was Pera Matišić, from a well-known Croatian musical family, with whom he had a son, Josip. Pera died in 1919 from the Spanish flu.</p>

<p>His second marriage was to a woman from the Budić family. They had a son, Martin, who was killed near Bihać in 1942 and never married.</p>

<p>His third marriage was to Joza Dragun, with no children.</p>

<h3>Josip Jurin</h3>

<p>Josip married Anica Dragun. They had two sons, Ivan and Milan, and four daughters: Slava, Mara, Neda, and Maca.</p>

<h3>Ivan Josipov</h3>

<p>Ivan married twice.</p>

<p>From his first marriage to Matija Pušić, he had two sons, Jure and Vladimir, and a daughter, Mihaela (baptized Milena).</p>

<p>Jure married Ruža Kosić and they have two sons: Ivica Julio and Marin Tin.</p>

<p>Vladimir married Ljubica Kosić and they have two sons: Filip and Leo.</p>

<p>This is an example of two brothers marrying two sisters.</p>

<p>From his second marriage to Verka Nikolovski, Ivan had no children.</p>

<p>Ivan died in Zagreb in 2025 at the age of 93.</p>

<p><em>May he rest in peace.</em></p>

<h3>Mijo Antin</h3>

<p>Mijo, the second son of Ante, married Manda Martinović. They had nine children: Jozo, Ante, Mate, Mijo, Petar, Iva, Matija, Ruža, and Antica.</p>

<p>No further information exists about his son Mijo beyond the birth record. It is assumed he either died young or moved away.</p>

<p>Descendants through Jozo, Mate, and Petar are known as <strong>Tucići</strong>, a nickname given due to the family’s reputation for romantic adventures.</p>    
  
<h3>Jozo Mijin</h3>

<p>Jozo married Iva Bilojelić. They had three sons: Mate, Jozo, and Nikola (who died at age six), and four daughters: Matija, Jela, Mara, and Iva.</p>

<h3>Jozo Jozin</h3>

<p>Jozo never married.</p>

<h3>Ante Jozin</h3>

<p>Ante married Jela Škorić. They had four sons: Marijan, Mate, Pilip, and Nikola, and four daughters: Jela, Mara, Kata, and Mila.</p>

<h3>Marijan Antin (Đika)</h3>

<p>Marijan married Iva Čorbić. They had two sons, Ivan and Milan, and four daughters: Mara, Dragica, Kata, and Marija.</p>

<h3>Ivan Marijanov (Đikin)</h3>

<p>Ivan married Ana Pušić. They have a son, Zdenko, and a daughter, Kristina.</p>

<p>Zdenko married twice. From his first marriage he has a son, Tomislav.</p>

<p>From his second marriage to Kristina Topić, he has a daughter, Ana.</p>

<h3>Milan Marijanov (Đikin)</h3>

<p>Milan married twice.</p>

<p>From his first marriage to Marija Pušić, he has a son, Nedjeljko, and three daughters: Dragica, Ljubica, and Tanja.</p>

<p>Nedjeljko and Ivana Božičević have two daughters, Marija and Tina.</p>

<p>Milan had no children from his second marriage.</p>

<h3>Mate Antin</h3>

<p>Mate, another son of Ante, married Matija Gudelj. They had no children.</p>

<h3>Marijan Antin</h3>

<p>The youngest son of Ante, Marijan married Maša Gudelj and had one son, Ante.</p>

<p>Ante married Renata Nagy and had a son also named Ante.</p>

<p>Ante Antin and his wife Valentina Juriša also had a son named Ante.</p>

<p>It is notable that three consecutive generations gave their sons the same name, Ante.</p>

<h3>Ante Mijin</h3>

<p>Ante never married and died at the age of 26.</p>

<h3>Mate Mijin</h3>

<p>Mate married twice.</p>

<p>From his first marriage to Tomica Kovač, he had a son Ivan, who died at age seven.</p>

<p>From his second marriage to Iva Vlajčić, he had two sons, Martin and Jure, and a daughter, Iva.</p>

<p>Martin died at the age of 24.</p>

<h3>Jure Matin (Đuka)</h3>

<p>Jure married Matija Škorić. They had two sons, Ante and Mate, and three daughters: Mila, Stana, and Iva.</p>

<h3>Ante Jurin</h3>

<p>Ante married Mila Đikić. They had three sons: Ivan, Milan, and Srećko, and one daughter, Matija.</p>

<p>Milan and Srećko are married, each with two sons. They live in Đakovo.</p>

<h3>Mate Jurin</h3>

<p>Mate married Danica Malenica. They have one son, Tomislav, and three daughters: Marija, Mila, and Ana.</p>

<p>Tomislav married Vlatka Dolić. They have a son Matej and a daughter Danijela. They live in Podstrana near Split.</p>

<h3>Petar Mijin</h3>

<p>Petar, the youngest son of Mijo, married Matija Tandara. They had four sons: Mate, Stipan, Ante (who died as a child), and Ilija, and one daughter, Anđa.</p>

<h3>Mate Petrov</h3>

<p>Mate married Kata Cimerman. They had one son, Ivan, and one daughter, Ankica.</p>

<h3>Ivan Matin</h3>

<p>Ivan married Pavica Kralik. They had a son Emil and a daughter Ivana.</p>

<p>Emil married Zorica Nađ. They have two daughters, Marijana and Nikolina. They live in Kutjevo and are known for wine production.</p>

<h3>Stipan Petrov</h3>

<p>Stipan married Joza Malenica. They had one son Ivan and one daughter Ankica.</p>

<h3>Ivan Stipanov</h3>

<p>Ivan married Ana Budimir. They had one son Mirko and three daughters: Mirjana, Marija, and Ankica.</p>

<p>Mirko married Dragica Čamber. They have two sons, Ivan and Josip, and one daughter, Ana Marija. They live in Dugo Selo.</p>

<h3>Ilija Petrov (Grabunjaš)</h3>

<p>Ilija, the youngest son of Petar, married Anica Škorić. They had two sons, Marijan and Mirko, and three daughters: Maca, Neda, and Dragica.</p>

<h3>Marijan Ilijin (Marinko Grabunjašev)</h3>

<p>Marijan married Franka Kovač. They had two sons, Nediljko (who died as a child) and Mirčo, and three daughters: Ivanka, Marija, and Neda.</p>

<p>Mirčo and his wife Vesna Zetović have a son, Miroslav, and a daughter, Sonja. They live in Đakovo.</p>

<h3>Mirko Ilijin (Grabunjašev)</h3>

<p>Mirko married Kata Kovač. They had three sons, Marinko, Ivica, and Ante, and two daughters, Anka and Marija.</p>

<p>Marinko, Ivica, and Ante live in Zagreb and have families.</p>   
    
<h2>Sub-branch of Filip, son of Ante</h2>

<h3>Filip Antin</h3>

<p>Filip, the second son of Ante, remained living in Ričice. In 1802 he married Matija Parlov. They had three sons: Martin, Mate, and Ivan, and five daughters: Joza, Jela, Jurka, Antica, and Ruža. For Mate and Ivan, only birth records exist, suggesting they either died young or moved away.</p>

<h3>Martin Filipov</h3>

<p>Martin married Manda Manenica. They had five sons: Jerko, Ilija, Ivan, Martin, and Ivan (younger), and three daughters: Tomica, Lucija, and Iva.</p>

<p>The elder Ivan and Martin died in childhood. No records exist for the younger Ivan, suggesting he either died young or emigrated.</p>

<h3>Jerko Martinov</h3>

<p>Jerko married Iva Topalušić. They had three sons: Martin, Luka (who died as a child), and Ivan.</p>

<h3>Martin Jerkov</h3>

<p>Martin married Iva Kovač. They had three daughters: Matija, Mara, and Iva.</p>

<h3>Ivan Jerkov</h3>

<p>Ivan married Jaka Martinović. They had two sons, Mate and Martin, and two daughters, Ana and Tomica.</p>

<h3>Mate Ivanov (Pikić)</h3>

<p>Born in 1898, Mate moved to his mother’s estate in Martinovići. He married Matija Ležeta, and his descendants are known by the nickname <strong>Pikići</strong>.</p>

<p>It is said of Mate: “Such a man could not even be born from a mother who did not try hard.” From this saying, he earned the nickname Piko, and his descendants became known as Pikići.</p>

<p>Mate and Matija had three sons: Nikola, Mirko, and Marijan, and two daughters: Milica and Dragica.</p>

<h3>Nikola Matin</h3>

<p>Nikola married Matija Kilić. They had two sons, Damir and Željko, and two daughters, Vera and Marija.</p>

<h3>Damir Nikolin</h3>

<p>Damir married twice.</p>

<p>From his first marriage to Marina Čelan, he had a son, Tin.</p>

<p>From his second marriage to Lucija Modrić, he had a son, Leo, and two daughters, Žana and Doris.</p>

<p>Damir and his family live in Germany.</p>

<h3>Željko Nikolin</h3>

<p>Željko married Anita Košćak. They have two sons, Nikola and Marko. They live in Split.</p>

<h3>Mirko Matin</h3>

<p>Mirko, the second son of Mate, married Anđelka Dragica Mršić. They had three sons: Nedjeljko, Zdravko, and Miroslav.</p>

<h3>Nedjeljko Mirkov</h3>

<p>Nedjeljko married Danica Jaginović. They had three sons: Mirko, Ivan, and Križan.</p>

<h3>Zdravko Mirkov</h3>

<p>Zdravko married Dubravka Brajković. They had two sons: Ante and Vedran.</p>

<h3>Miroslav Mirkov</h3>

<p>Miroslav, the youngest son of Mirko, married Ružica Krajinović. They have a son Josip and two daughters, Ines and Ana. The family lives in Split.</p>

<h3>Marijan (third son of Mate)</h3>

<p>Marijan married Mara Tandara. They had a son, Mate, and a daughter, Snježana.</p>

<p>Mate married Zdravka Guić. They have three sons: Marijan, Ivan, and Ante. The family lives in Split.</p>

<h3>Martin (younger son of Ivan)</h3>

<p>Martin married Anica Lekić. They had three sons: Ivan, Jerko, and Marijan (who died as a child), and two daughters: Mara (who died at the age of five from burns) and Matija.</p>

<h3>Ivan Martinov</h3>

<p>Ivan married Ana Radmanić. They have a son, Darko, who is married to Dragica (née Sabolović). They have a son Ivan and a daughter Monika. They live in Bjelovar.</p>

<h3>Jerko (younger son of Martin)</h3>

<p>Jerko married Ružica Sekulić. They have a son, Renato, who married Tanja Lancoš and has a daughter, Lea. They live in Zagreb.</p>

<h3>Ilija (second son of Martin and Manda Manenica)</h3>

<p>Ilija was married to Luca Tavra. They had three sons: Mate, Ivan, and Šimun, and three daughters: Tomica, Iva, and Mara.</p>

<p>Ivan died at the age of six, and Šimun died as a small child.</p>

<h3>Mate Ilijin (Rumić branch)</h3>

<p>Mate reportedly had a very reddish complexion and was therefore nicknamed <strong>Rumić</strong>, and his descendants became known as Rumići.</p>

<p>Mate married Mara Topalušić. They had four sons: Ivan, Božo, Mijo, and Toma, and two daughters: Tomica and Mara.</p>

<p>No further records exist for Ivan and Božo apart from their birth entries, suggesting they either died young or moved away.</p>

<h3>Mijo Matin</h3>

<p>Mijo married Joza Štrljić. They had two sons, Vinko and Milan.</p>

<h3>Vinko (older son of Mijo)</h3>

<p>Vinko married twice. From his first marriage to Krsta Mršić, he had five sons: Mijo, Ante, Milan, Zdravko, and Vinko.</p>

<p>From his second marriage to Matija Sičenica, Vinko had no children.</p>

<h3>Mijo (eldest son of Vinko)</h3>

<p>Mijo married Jelena Krezo. They had two sons: Ivica and Zoran.</p>

<p>Zoran married Vesna Belan. They have a son, Luka, and a daughter, Mija. The family lives in Germany.</p>

<h3>Ante (second son of Vinko)</h3>

<p>Ante married Vesna Topalušić. They have three daughters: Kristina, Marina, and Nikolina. They live in Germany.</p>

<h3>Milan (third son of Vinko)</h3>

<p>Milan married Nediljka Matušić. They had three sons: Kristijan, Antonio, and Dino, and one daughter, Valentina. They live in Predavac near Bjelovar.</p>

<h3>Zdravko (fourth son of Vinko)</h3>

<p>Zdravko married Brigita Horvatinčić. They had two sons, Mate and Bruno, and two daughters, Anita and Petra. They live in Predavac near Bjelovar.</p>

<h3>Vinko (fifth son of Vinko)</h3>

<p>Vinko married Slavica Matišić. They had a son, Mario, and a daughter, Marina. They live in Predavac near Bjelovar.</p>

<h3>Milan (younger son of Mijo)</h3>

<p>Milan married Iva Lukić. They had two sons, Željko and Dragan, and two daughters, Rosa and Dragica.</p>

<h3>Toma Matin</h3>

<p>The youngest son of Mate and Mara Topalušić, Toma married Tomica Tandara. They had five sons: Petar, Marijan (killed in WWII), Slavko, Ante, and Mate, and four daughters: Mila, Dragica, Ana, and Nevenka.</p>

<h3>Petar Tomin</h3>

<p>Petar, the eldest son of Toma, married Kata Novosel. They had one son, Ivica.</p>

<p>Ivica married Ljubica Kozić. They have a son, Hrvoje, and a daughter, Sabina, a well-known Croatian journalist working at RTL. The family lives in Zagreb.</p>

<h3>Slavko Tomin</h3>

<p>Slavko, the third son of Toma, from his marriage to Savka Vukobratović, had a son, Marko. They live in Zagreb.</p>

<h3>Ante Tomin</h3>

<p>Ante, the fourth son of Toma, married Zlata Vučemil. They had a son, Draženko.</p>

<p>Draženko married Nada Medić. They have a son, Luka, and two daughters, Maja and Mateja. They live in Bjelovar.</p>

<h3>Mate Tomin</h3>

<p>Mate, the youngest son of Toma, married Tonka Vukičević. They had a son, Željko.</p>

<p>Željko married Ankica Šitum. They have two sons and live in Canada.</p>    

